 },
 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "RankedCache(capacity, source) wraps a slow data source given as rows [key, value, rank] with unique keys (copied, never modified). put(key, value, rank) on a key already cached replaces its value and rank. On a new key when the cache already holds capacity entries, it first evicts the entry with the smallest rank; among equal ranks, the one whose last write is oldest (the preview allows any, so this tie rule is chosen for determinism). get never changes the cache order. put also writes the entry through to the data source. get(key) returns the cached value; on a miss it loads the key from the data source when present (counting one load and inserting it into the cache exactly like a put of its stored value and rank, without writing back) and returns the value, otherwise returns \"\". getLoadCount() returns the number of loads so far. Every method call is answered in call order on one instance; void methods return nothing.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk10-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
    "sha256": "be5d798382a43847401e76609d79932746e664be0d91c81b132bf6b46cd69126",
    "selector": "/problems/4/inferred_spec"
   }
  ]
 },
